    <td>Major depressive disorder, recurrent, severe, without psychotic features (second episode; structured diagnostic interview; MDQ negative and no past hypomanic or manic episode on interview)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F33.2</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis anchored to his documented depression after the 1955 breakdown (D); the bipolar interpretation (R) is addressed and not adopted.</td>
